--TEST--
a shape alias whose field names the alias itself is one `E0310` at the alias, and an alias cycle is one `E0310` with no `E0307` beside it — `rule:types/type-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/type-alias`: a cycle is a diagnostic. A shape field is a type
// position like any other, so `Node` naming itself in `next` is a cycle of
// one, reported once where `Node` is declared.
type Node = {value: int, next: ?Node};

// `A` and `B` name each other and no class, so the cycle is the one error.
type A = B;
type B = A;

// An alias naming another alias is accepted.
type Id = int|string;
type Key = Id;

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0310]: type alias cycle: Node -> Node never bottoms out in a concrete type
  --> case.nvs:5:6
%A
error[E0310]: type alias cycle: A -> B -> A never bottoms out in a concrete type
  --> case.nvs:8:6
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
